// Rule: [T1059.001][T1105] STAC4749 - Teams Vishing Powershell Payload
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1059.001, T1105
// Classification: Hunting query
// Status: Untested implementation sketch
// Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR
// Required telemetry: DeviceProcessEvents
// Purpose: Source-observed PowerShell staging into AppData\Roaming followed by tokenized implant launch.
// Logic: Evaluate DeviceProcessEvents for teams vishing powershell payload using the existing source-derived conditions while preserving projected investigation context.
// A match proves: A source-observed PowerShell staging pattern occurred on the endpoint and requires authorization and payload review.
// A match does not prove: Successful C2, malware identity, ransomware deployment, data theft or attribution.
// Expected false positives: authorized administration, approved software, testing, or benign artifact collisions.
// Coverage limits: local schema, field population, retention, collection scope, and attacker variation require validation.
// Evidence claims: C001, C002, C003
//
// STAC4749 PowerShell payload retrieval and tokenized implant launch
// Classification: Hunting query - Untested implementation sketch
// Confidence: Medium
// Platform: Microsoft Defender XDR Advanced Hunting
// Telemetry prerequisite: Microsoft Defender for Endpoint populating DeviceProcessEvents
// Evidence: Sophos observed this command pattern in STAC4749 incidents (Feb-Jun 2026).
// This campaign-specific hunt is not suitable for alerting until benign overlap is measured.
DeviceProcessEvents
| where FileName in~ ("powershell.exe", "pwsh.exe")
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "Invoke-WebRequest"
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "-OutFile"
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "--token-raw"
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "Start-Process"
| where ProcessCommandLine contains @"\AppData\Roaming\"
| project Timestamp, DeviceId, DeviceName, AccountUpn, AccountName,
          FileName, FolderPath, ProcessCommandLine,
          InitiatingProcessFileName, InitiatingProcessCommandLine,
          ProcessId, ProcessUniqueId, ReportId
| order by Timestamp desc
